# Site-wide security headers.
#
# Referrer-Policy is the important one: share tokens travel in the URL query
# (?t=, ?deck=<id>&token=, ?collection=<uuid>&token=). strict-origin-when-cross-
# origin stops the full URL (with token) from leaking in the Referer header to
# third parties on outbound navigations (TCGPlayer affiliate links, the YouTube
# embed, the QR image service). frame-ancestors/X-Frame-Options stop the
# authenticated, mutating UI from being clickjacked inside a hostile iframe.
#
# NOTE: the Content-Security-Policy is a full, script-restricting policy and it
# is ENFORCED (see the rollout history below). The app is a single no-build
# Index.html with inline scripts and inline styles, so script-src still needs
# 'unsafe-inline'; everything else collapses to 'self' plus the named origins
# because the core libs are VENDORED same-origin (see Index.html /vendor/*).
#
# ROLLOUT HISTORY: 2026-07-14 shipped as `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`
# (blocks nothing, reports every would-be violation to Sentry via the
# report-uri at the end — check Issues for "CSP" security events).
#
# ENFORCED as of 2026-09-05 (audit follow-up, Zaven's call). Report-only had run
# since 2026-07-14 and, after the 08-10 / 08-22 fixes below, every remaining
# report in Sentry was noise: one client on a stale service worker still
# carrying the pre-08-10 policy, browser extensions (connect.facebook.net,
# eval:), a local dev server framing the site, and the Netlify preview
# toolbar. The single enforced header below IS the full policy (the old
# "lite" frame-ancestors/object-src/base-uri line is folded into it) and it
# keeps the report-uri, so a genuine block still shows up in Sentry as a CSP
# issue — that is the signal to add an origin, redeploy, and purge.
# ROLLBACK: rename the header back to Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only
# (keep the frame-ancestors line enforced separately), deploy, purge.
#
# Two per-path exceptions below, both detach-and-replace: /swiss (frame-ancestors
# 'self' so the Analytics tab can embed it) and /scanner-worker.js ('unsafe-eval'
# for OpenCV). Everything else on the site runs the /* policy.
# Known residual (Sentry JAVASCRIPT-12): after the 08-10 fix the ONLY img-src
# reports came from one Securly-filtered network (every document URI carries the
# filter's ?scrlybrkr= cache-breaker) and name same-origin /img-proxy/ card art.
# 'self' cannot fail on its own URL — that is the filter redirecting the image
# request off-origin, and Chrome reports the pre-redirect URL. Not a policy gap,
# and nothing in the allow-list can fix it.
#
# Historical note — STILL REPORT-ONLY as of 2026-08-10. Sentry review that day found two real
# gaps, both fixed below — supabase card art in img-src (3,053 reports / 183
# users, i.e. blank pre-staged art for everyone had this been enforced) and the
# Cloudflare beacon in script-/connect-src (201 reports / 52 users, new since
# the cutover). DON'T enforce on the strength of that fix alone: two reporters
# also logged img-src/connect-src blocks against packs.ink ITSELF under 'self'
# (Sentry JAVASCRIPT-12/-13), on documents carrying a `?scrlybrkr=` param this
# app never generates — almost certainly a browser extension or filtering proxy
# rewriting URLs, but unexplained. Give it another week of report-only and
# confirm those two stay flat before renaming the header.
# The _headers file does NOT take effect on the local dev server — verify on a
# Netlify Deploy Preview or prod.
# Origins below were enumerated from Index.html + sw.js (2026-06-27 audit):
#   script:  self (vendored libs) + sentry loader (js.sentry-cdn.com) + the SDK
#            bundle the loader pulls (browser.sentry-cdn.com) + cdnjs (artist-
#            poster html2canvas) + jsdelivr (scanner workers importScripts
#            opencv.js + onnxruntime) + 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (scanner WASM)
#            + static.cloudflareinsights.com — Cloudflare injects its Web
#            Analytics beacon into every response since the 2026-08-04 cutover,
#            so it is ours by deployment even though no repo file references it.
#            Drop it here if Web Analytics is ever turned off in the dashboard.
#   style:   self + Google Fonts CSS;  font: self + gstatic
#   img:     self + data:/blob: (LOGO_B64, canvas exports) + lorcast/tcgplayer/
#            qrserver/ravensburger.cloud/ebay/google-photo CDNs + the supabase
#            host: /storage/v1/object/public/card-art/* serves PRE-STAGED card
#            art and pack arts as plain <img> src, which is an img-src load, not
#            the connect-src one PostgREST makes. Both directives need the host.
#   connect: self + data: + supabase (https+wss) + zippopotam + ravensburgerplay
#            + sentry ingest/CDN + Google Fonts (googleapis+gstatic) + the cross-
#            origin IMAGE CDNs. The image/font/sentry-cdn HOSTS appear here (not
#            just in img-/font-/style-/script-src) because the service worker
#            intercepts every cross-origin request and re-fetches it via fetch()
#            (images per destination==="image"; fonts/CSS/other via the stale-
#            while-revalidate branch, sw.js ~line 164) — a fetch() from the SW
#            context is classified as connect-src, NOT its resource directive.
#            The offline image downloader (Index.html startOfflineImagePack)
#            fetches the same image hosts from the page. Without these, enforcing
#            the policy would break card-art caching, web-font loading, the Sentry
#            loader, and the offline downloader (report-only today).
#   NOTE: the report-only 'eval:' violations (Sentry "JAVASCRIPT-R") come from
#            browser-extension-injected scripts, NOT this app — no repo code uses
#            eval/new Function. Do NOT add 'unsafe-eval' to accommodate them; the
#            scanner/ONNX + exports only need 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (already set).
#   frame:   'self' (the Analytics » Swiss Odds tab iframes /swiss?embed=1 —
#            without it, enforcing would re-break the embed from the parent
#            side) + youtube embeds — deck pages use www.youtube-nocookie.com
#            (privacy-enhanced mode, no cookie until playback) since the
#            2026-09-05 audit; www.youtube.com stays listed for any document
#            still cached from before;  worker: self + blob: (scanner + canvas
#            workers)
#   qrserver: api.qrserver.com is still listed in img-/connect-src for
#            documents cached from before 2026-09-05; the deck-poster QR is
#            now drawn locally (vendor/qrcode.js) so no share URL — and no
#            Unlisted-deck token — leaves the origin. Drop the host once
#            every client has cycled past CACHE_VERSION packsink-v373.
#   frame-ancestors 'none' lives in the enforced policy (with the 'self'
#            carve-out in the /swiss block below). While the policy was
#            report-only it was kept OUT of the RO copy, because Chrome logs
#            and reports RO frame-ancestors violations — every Swiss Odds tab
#            view produced a false-positive Sentry report (removed 2026-08-22).
#            Never put frame-ancestors back into a Report-Only header.
/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://js.sentry-cdn.com https://browser.sentry-cdn.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co https://cards.lorcast.io https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com https://api.qrserver.com https://ravensburger.cloud https://*.ebayimg.com https://lh3.googleusercontent.com; connect-src 'self' data: https://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co wss://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://api.zippopotam.us https://tcg.ravensburgerplay.com https://api.ravensburgerplay.com https://tcgcsv.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://js.sentry-cdn.com https://browser.sentry-cdn.com https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.sentry.io https://fonts.googleapis.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cards.lorcast.io https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com https://api.qrserver.com https://ravensburger.cloud https://*.ebayimg.com https://lh3.googleusercontent.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com https://youtu.be; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; report-uri https://o4511390961303552.ingest.us.sentry.io/api/4511390972444672/security/?sentry_key=8eb7cada506131426389fd7506a0288e
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(self)
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# The Analytics » Swiss Odds tab embeds the sim same-origin:
# <iframe src="/swiss?embed=1"> in Index.html. The site-wide clickjacking
# block above (X-Frame-Options: DENY + frame-ancestors 'none') refuses
# framing even from packs.ink itself, so the embed rendered as the browser's
# gray broken-page icon on prod (found live 2026-08-21; invisible in local
# dev, which doesn't apply this file). SAMEORIGIN / 'self' keeps hostile-site
# framing blocked while letting the app frame its own page. The Report-Only
# policy needs no override here because it no longer carries frame-ancestors
# at all (Chrome logs+reports RO frame-ancestors violations, contrary to the
# spec's SHOULD-ignore — observed live; the enforced lite policy is what
# actually guards framing).
# The full enforced policy is mirrored here verbatim with the one difference
# frame-ancestors 'self' (2026-09-05). Keep the two policies identical apart
# from that directive: an origin added to /* must be added here too, or the
# embedded Swiss page silently loses it.
/swiss
  ! X-Frame-Options
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://js.sentry-cdn.com https://browser.sentry-cdn.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co https://cards.lorcast.io https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com https://api.qrserver.com https://ravensburger.cloud https://*.ebayimg.com https://lh3.googleusercontent.com; connect-src 'self' data: https://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co wss://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://api.zippopotam.us https://tcg.ravensburgerplay.com https://api.ravensburgerplay.com https://tcgcsv.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://js.sentry-cdn.com https://browser.sentry-cdn.com https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.sentry.io https://fonts.googleapis.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cards.lorcast.io https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com https://api.qrserver.com https://ravensburger.cloud https://*.ebayimg.com https://lh3.googleusercontent.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com https://youtu.be; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; report-uri https://o4511390961303552.ingest.us.sentry.io/api/4511390972444672/security/?sentry_key=8eb7cada506131426389fd7506a0288e

# The OpenCV worker needs 'unsafe-eval'. @techstark/opencv-js 4.10 is an
# Emscripten/embind build whose createNamedFunction and makeDynCaller go
# through `new Function` — Sentry JAVASCRIPT-R: 9 reports from 3 users in 90
# days, every one of them from scanner-worker.js with source_file
# cdn.jsdelivr.net/.../opencv.js line 30. Under the enforced /* policy that is a
# throw during cv init, i.e. every scan session dead on arrival. A dedicated
# worker loaded from a URL is governed by the policy delivered with ITS OWN
# script response (CSP3 "Workers"), not the page's, so the relaxation is
# confined to this one file — the page and the OCR worker (vendor/ort has no
# eval) keep the strict policy. Minimal on purpose: the worker only imports
# opencv from jsdelivr, decodes the embedded base64 wasm (Emscripten fetches a
# data: URI for it, hence data: in connect-src) and talks over postMessage.
# The path match ignores the ?v= the page appends.
# Verified 2026-09-05 under wrangler dev + Playwright (opencv served from the
# npm tarball, headers real): with this block the worker posts {type:'ready'}
# and answers a capture round-trip; a byte-identical copy served under the /*
# policy, or under this block minus 'unsafe-eval', dies inside importScripts.
/scanner-worker.js
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; connect-src 'self' data: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; report-uri https://o4511390961303552.ingest.us.sentry.io/api/4511390972444672/security/?sentry_key=8eb7cada506131426389fd7506a0288e

# NOTE (2026-09-05 audit): the two proxy blocks below are INERT on Cloudflare.
# Workers Assets applies _headers only to responses it serves from dist/; the
# /img-proxy/* and /tcg-img-proxy/* responses are built by worker/index.js,
# which sets the same Cache-Control + ACAO itself. Kept as documentation of
# the intended headers (and for any host that applies _headers natively).
#
# Long-cache + permissive CORS on proxied Lorcast art.
#
# Lorcast (cards.lorcast.io) sends no Cache-Control header, so without an
# override Netlify edge treats the response as uncacheable — every miss
# forwards to Lorcast and pulls bandwidth across both legs of the proxy.
# A 30-day immutable cache lets Netlify's CDN absorb almost the entire
# load: each edge POP fetches once, then serves locally for a month.
# Image URLs are content-addressed (Lorcast appends a hash query param when
# they re-publish), so a long cache won't trap stale art — a new card
# revision arrives at a new URL the catalog ETL picks up.
#
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * guarantees canvas exports (deck poster,
# card poster, mover-tile) stay untainted no matter what Lorcast does with
# their CORS headers later. The browser only enforces CORS on
# crossOrigin="anonymous" <img>s — same-origin requests ignore it — but
# pinning ACAO is free insurance.
/img-proxy/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Same treatment for proxied TCGPlayer art (sealed products + Lorcast-unindexed
# promo/extras cards). The ACAO matters for the native (Capacitor) app builds,
# which load these proxies cross-origin from https://localhost with
# crossOrigin="anonymous" — without it those loads fail outright. Inert for the
# web (same-origin requests ignore CORS headers).
/tcg-img-proxy/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
